-- title:
--   The hard kernel agrees almost everywhere with the open annulus kernel
-- statement:
--   For $r\le R$, the sharply truncated kernel $H_{r,R}(t)=\dfrac{\mathbf 1_{r<|t|}-\mathbf 1_{R<|t|}}t$ satisfies
--   $$
--   H_{r,R}(t)=\mathbf 1_{\{r<|t|<R\}}(t)\,\frac1t\qquad\text{for almost every }t\in\mathbb R .
--   $$
--
--   So truncated integrals over the open annulus $\{r<|t|<R\}$, as in the maximal triangular Hilbert transform, can be computed with the hard kernel.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/TriangularHilbert/Coordinates.lean#L45-L65

